# Batch files are parsed line-by-line by cmd.exe and MUST be CRLF. With LF-only
# endings every `REM comment` line executes as the command `M`, which is exactly
# how scripts/collect_recurrence.cmd failed the first time it ran. Checked out
# with CRLF regardless of the platform's default.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# PowerShell is tolerant of LF, but keeping the Windows-only scripts consistent
# means one rule to remember rather than two.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
